# Citation metadata of ZNN-Bench 1.0.0 (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# Add `doi:` and `repository-code:` once the archive and the repository are published.
# Author names are given exactly as supplied (entity form); split them into given-names and
# family-names if preferred.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ZNN-Bench, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "ZNN-Bench: an open, step-size-resolved benchmark of zeroing and gradient neural dynamics"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "Phat T. Tran-Truong"
  - name: "Phien Nguyen-Ngoc"
  - name: "Ha X. Son"
  - name: "Tran Gia Huy"
  - name: "Khanh H. Vo"
  - name: "Triet M. Nguyen"
  - name: "Nhan T. K. Nguyen"
  - name: "Thuc M. Nguyen"
abstract: >-
  ZNN-Bench is an open Python benchmark of zeroing neural networks (ZNN) and gradient neural
  networks for time-varying problems. It implements problems, models, activations, gain schedules,
  difference formulas, noise models and information regimes from the literature, runs sweeps over the
  sampling period and the step size, and contains the configurations, logged results and analysis
  scripts of its full-scale experiments, together with the material of a reporting-practice
  meta-analysis of open-access ZNN publications.
keywords:
  - zeroing neural network
  - gradient neural network
  - time-varying problem
  - discretization
  - step size
  - benchmark
